我想简短地回应一下。

1131
01:18:29,824 --> 01:18:34,787
Clearly, I am not Joe Biden, and I am certainly not Donald Trump.
显然，我不是乔·拜登，当然也不是唐纳德·特朗普。

1132
01:18:35,647 --> 01:18:51,417
And what I do offer is a new generation of leadership for our country, one who believes in what is possible, one who brings a sense of optimism about what we can do instead of always disparaging the American people.
我提供的是我们国家新一代的领导力，一个相信可能性的人，一个带来乐观态度的人，而不是总是贬低美国人民。

1133
01:18:52,237 --> 01:18:54,058
I believe in what we can do to
我相信我们能做些什么

1134
01:18:55,379 --> 01:18:58,763
to strengthen our small businesses, which is why I have a plan.
来加强我们的小企业，这就是为什么我有一个计划。

1135
01:18:58,803 --> 01:19:03,327
Let's talk about our plans and let's compare the plans.
让我们谈谈我们的计划，并比较一下这些计划。

1136
01:19:03,888 --> 01:19:08,253
I have a plan to give startup businesses $50,000 tax deduction
我有一个计划，为初创企业提供5万美元的税收减免

1137
01:19:10,635 --> 01:19:15,858
to pursue their ambitions, their innovation, their ideas, their hard work.
以追求他们的抱负、创新、想法和辛勤工作。

1138
01:19:16,098 --> 01:19:26,062
I have a plan, $6,000 for young families for the first year of your child's life to help you in that most critical stage of your child's development.
我有一个计划，为年轻家庭提供6000美元，用于孩子生命的第一年，帮助你在孩子发展的最关键阶段。

1139
01:19:26,262 --> 01:19:27,123
I have a plan.
我有一个计划。

1140
01:19:27,763 --> 01:19:41,516
That is about allowing people to be able to pursue what has been fleeting in terms of the American dream by offering a help with down payment of $25,000 down payment assistance for first-time home buyers.
这是为了让人们能够追求那些在美国梦中所缺失的东西，通过提供2.5万美元的首付援助，帮助首次购房者。

1141
01:19:42,076 --> 01:19:52,605
That's the kind of conversation, I believe, David, that people really want tonight, as opposed to a conversation that is constantly about belittling and name-calling.
我认为，大卫，这才是人们今晚真正想要的对话，而不是那种总是贬低和谩骂的对话。

1142
01:19:53,346 --> 01:19:55,188
Let's turn the page and move forward.
让我们翻开新的一页，继续前进。

1143
01:19:55,208 --> 01:19:56,129
President Trump, we have to move on.
特朗普总统，我们得继续了。

1144
01:19:56,189 --> 01:19:57,290
She has a plan to defund the police.
她有一个计划要削减警察经费。

1145
01:19:57,310 --> 01:19:58,971
She has a plan to confiscate everybody's gun.
她有一个计划要没收所有人的枪。

1146
01:19:59,011 --> 01:20:01,394
President Trump, we do have to move on to other issues.
特朗普总统，我们确实得继续讨论其他问题了。

1147
01:20:10,542 --> 01:20:12,603
in Pennsylvania or anywhere else.
在宾夕法尼亚州或其他任何地方。

1148
01:20:12,623 --> 01:20:15,184
That's what her plan is until just recently.
这就是她最近的计划。

1149
01:20:15,445 --> 01:20:20,147
The former president has said something twice that I need to respond to.
前总统说了两次我需要回应的话。

1150
01:20:20,187 --> 01:20:23,028
I just need to respond one time to what he has said multiple times.
我只需要回应一次他多次说过的话。

1151
01:20:23,049 --> 01:20:26,190
President Trump, this is now your third time running for president.
特朗普总统，这是你第三次竞选总统了。

1152
01:20:26,250 --> 01:20:31,413
You have long vowed to repeal and replace the Affordable Care Act, also known as Obamacare.
你曾长期誓言要废除并取代《平价医疗法案》，也就是奥巴马医改。

1153
01:20:31,433 --> 01:20:32,854
You have failed to accomplish that.
但你未能实现这一目标。

1154
01:20:33,194 --> 01:20:37,436
You now say you're going to keep Obamacare, quote, unless we can do something much better.
你现在说你会保留奥巴马医改，除非我们能做得更好。

1155
01:20:37,936 --> 01:20:40,097
Last month, you said, quote, we're working on it.
上个月，你说，我们在努力。

1156
01:20:40,417 --> 01:20:46,199
So tonight, nine years after you first started running, do you have a plan and can you tell us what it is?
所以今晚，在你第一次竞选九年后，你有一个计划吗？你能告诉我们是什么吗？

1157
01:20:46,319 --> 01:20:49,260
Obamacare was lousy health care, always was.
奥巴马医改的医疗保健一直很糟糕。

1158
01:20:49,640 --> 01:20:50,780
It's not very good today.
今天也不怎么样。

1159
01:20:51,481 --> 01:20:56,982
And what I said, that if we come up with something and we are working on things, we're going to do it and we're going to replace it.
我说过，如果我们能想出更好的方案，我们就会去做，我们会取代它。

1160
01:20:57,042 --> 01:20:58,063
But remember this.
但记住这一点。

1161
01:20:58,823 --> 01:21:02,665
I inherited Obamacare because Democrats wouldn't change it.
我继承了奥巴马医改，因为民主党人不愿意改变它。

1162
01:21:02,705 --> 01:21:03,625
They wouldn't vote for it.
他们不会投票支持。

1163
01:21:03,985 --> 01:21:04,825
They were unanimous.
他们是一致的。

1164
01:21:04,865 --> 01:21:06,306
They wouldn't vote to change it.
他们不会投票改变它。

1165
01:21:06,686 --> 01:21:10,307
If they would have done that, we would have had a much better plan than Obamacare.
如果他们那样做了，我们会有比奥巴马医改好得多的计划。

1166
01:21:10,668 --> 01:21:13,469
But the Democrats came up, they wouldn't vote for it.
但民主党人不愿意投票支持。

1167
01:21:13,969 --> 01:21:15,870
I had a choice to make when I was president.
我当总统时面临一个选择。

1168
01:21:16,190 --> 01:21:21,792
Do I save it and make it as good as it can be, never going to be great, or do I let it rot?
我是保留它并尽可能改善它，尽管它永远不会变得很好，还是让它腐烂？

1169
01:21:22,492 --> 01:21:28,155
And I felt I had an obligation, even though politically it would have been good to just let it rot and let it go away.
我觉得我有责任，尽管从政治上讲，让它腐烂并消失会更好。

1170
01:21:28,795 --> 01:21:32,377
I decided, and I told my people, the top people, and they're very good people.
我决定，并告诉了我的高层人员，他们是非常优秀的人。

1171
01:21:32,397 --> 01:21:34,838
I have a lot of good people in this, that administration.
我有很多优秀的人在这个政府里。

1172
01:21:35,398 --> 01:21:36,439
We read about the bad ones.
我们读到了那些不好的。

1173
01:21:36,459 --> 01:21:38,640
We had some real bad ones too, and so do they.
我们也有一些真正糟糕的人，他们也一样。

1174
01:21:38,680 --> 01:21:39,680
They have really bad ones.
他们确实有一些很糟糕的人。

1175
01:21:39,700 --> 01:21:40,921
The difference is they don't get rid of them.
不同的是，他们没有把他们清除掉。

1176
01:21:40,941 --> 01:21:41,461
But let me just
但让我

1177
01:21:41,741 --> 01:21:42,141
explain.
解释一下。

1178
01:21:42,762 --> 01:21:43,922
I had a choice to make.
我面临一个选择。

1179
01:21:44,302 --> 01:21:47,104
Do I save it and make it as good as it can be?
我是要拯救它，让它变得尽可能好？

1180
01:21:47,504 --> 01:21:48,465
Or do I let it rot?
还是让它腐烂？

1181
01:21:49,005 --> 01:21:49,825
And I saved it.
我拯救了它。

1182
01:21:49,985 --> 01:21:51,026
I did the right thing.
我做了正确的事。

1183
01:21:51,466 --> 01:21:55,768
But it's still never going to be great, and it's too expensive for people.
但它永远不会变得伟大，而且对人们来说太昂贵了。

1184
01:21:56,289 --> 01:21:59,390
And what we will do is we're looking at different plans.
我们将要做的是，我们正在考虑不同的计划。

1185
01:21:59,791 --> 01:22:01,972
If we can come up with a plan that's going to cost
如果我们能制定出一个计划，这个计划将花费

1186
01:22:02,552 --> 01:22:09,758
our people, our population, less money, and be better healthcare than Obamacare, then I would absolutely do it.
我们的人民，我们的人口，更少的钱，并且比奥巴马医改更好的医疗保健，那么我绝对会去做。

1187
01:22:10,158 --> 01:22:13,061
But until then, I'd run it as good as it can be run.
但在那之前，我会尽可能好地运行它。

1188
01:22:13,341 --> 01:22:15,463
So, just a yes or no, you still do not have a plan?
所以，只是一个是或否，你仍然没有一个计划？

1189
01:22:15,863 --> 01:22:17,324
I have concepts of a plan.
我有计划的构想。

1190
01:22:17,985 --> 01:22:19,366
I'm not president right now.
我现在不是总统。

1191
01:22:19,806 --> 01:22:20,306
But if
但如果

1192
01:22:21,604 --> 01:22:22,845
We come up with something.
我们想出了什么。

1193
01:22:22,865 --> 01:22:26,748
I would only change it if we come up with something that's better and less expensive.
只有在我们想出了更好且更便宜的东西时，我才会改变它。

1194
01:22:27,108 --> 01:22:31,192
And there are concepts and options we have to do that.
我们有一些概念和选项可以做到这一点。

1195
01:22:31,512 --> 01:22:34,114
And you'll be hearing about it in the not-too-distant future.
你会在不久的将来听到关于它的消息。

1196
01:22:34,354 --> 01:22:41,620
Vice President Harris, in 2017, you supported Bernie Sanders' proposal to do away with private insurance and create a government-run healthcare system.
副总统哈里斯，在2017年，你支持伯尼·桑德斯的提议，取消私人保险，建立一个政府运营的医疗保健系统。

1197
01:22:42,041 --> 01:22:45,944
Two years later, you proposed a plan that included a private insurance option.
两年后，你提出了一项包括私人保险选项的计划。

1198
01:22:46,264 --> 01:22:47,185
What is your plan today?
你今天的计划是什么？

1199
01:22:47,745 --> 01:22:56,949
Well, first of all, I absolutely support, and over the last four years as vice president, private healthcare options, but what we need to do is maintain and grow the Affordable Care Act.
首先，我绝对支持，并且在过去四年作为副总统期间，支持私人医疗保健选项，但我们需要做的是维持并扩大《平价医疗法案》。

1200
01:22:56,969 --> 01:23:02,371
But I'll get to that, Lindsay, I just need to respond to a previous point that the former president has made.
但我会谈到那个，林赛，我需要回应前总统之前提出的一个观点。

1201
01:23:02,691 --> 01:23:07,453
I've made very clear my position on fracking, and then this business about taking everyone's guns away.
我已经非常明确地表明了我在水力压裂问题上的立场，然后是关于没收所有人枪支的事情。

1202
01:23:08,054 --> 01:23:09,554
Tim Walz and I are both gun owners.
蒂姆·沃尔兹和我都是枪支拥有者。

1203
01:23:09,594 --> 01:23:13,556
We're not taking anybody's guns away, so stop with the continuous lying about this stuff.
我们不会没收任何人的枪支，所以不要再继续撒谎了。

1204
01:23:14,614 --> 01:23:19,656
As it relates to the Affordable Care Act, understand, just look at the history to know where people stand.
关于《平价医疗法案》，了解历史就能知道人们的立场。

1205
01:23:20,076 --> 01:23:26,298
When Donald Trump was president, 60 times he tried to get rid of the Affordable Care Act.
当唐纳德·特朗普担任总统时，他试图废除《平价医疗法案》60次。

1206
01:23:26,318 --> 01:23:26,798
60 times.
60次。

1207
01:23:27,059 --> 01:23:36,302
I was a senator at the time when, I will never forget the early morning hours when it was up for a vote in the United States Senate.
我当时是参议员，我永远不会忘记那天凌晨，法案在美国参议院进行投票的时刻。

1208
01:23:36,762 --> 01:23:41,424
And the late, great John McCain, who you have disparaged,
还有已故的伟大人物约翰·麦凯恩，你曾贬低他，

1209
01:23:42,464 --> 01:23:47,928
as being, you don't like him, you said, at the time, because he got caught.
你说你不喜欢他，因为他在那时被抓住了把柄。

1210
01:23:48,028 --> 01:23:49,329
He was an American hero.
他是一位美国英雄。

1211
01:23:49,589 --> 01:23:56,454
The late, great John McCain, I will never forget that night, walked onto the Senate floor and said, no you don't.
已故的伟大人物约翰·麦凯恩，我永远不会忘记那个晚上，他走进参议院说，不，你不能。

1212
01:23:57,154 --> 01:23:57,755
No you don't.
不，你不能。

1213
01:23:58,255 --> 01:24:00,516
No, you don't get rid of the Affordable Care Act.
不，你不能废除《平价医疗法案》。

1214
01:24:00,536 --> 01:24:01,717
You have no plan.
你没有计划。

1215
01:24:02,358 --> 01:24:09,482
And what the Affordable Care Act has done is eliminate the ability of insurance companies to deny people with pre-existing conditions.
《平价医疗法案》所做的是消除了保险公司拒绝有预先存在条件的人的能力。

1216
01:24:09,962 --> 01:24:12,764
I don't have to tell the people watching tonight, you remember what that was like?
我不需要告诉今晚观看的观众，你们还记得那是什么样子吗？

1217
01:24:13,664 --> 01:24:16,046
Remember when an insurance company could deny
记得保险公司可以拒绝

1218
01:24:17,176 --> 01:24:23,559
if a child had asthma, if someone was a breast cancer survivor, if a grandparent had diabetes.
如果一个孩子有哮喘，如果有人是乳腺癌幸存者，如果祖父母有糖尿病。

1219
01:24:24,240 --> 01:24:36,446
And thankfully, as I've been vice president and we over the last four years have strengthened the Affordable Care Act, we have allowed for the first time Medicare to negotiate drug prices on behalf of you, the American people.
值得庆幸的是，作为副总统，我们在过去四年中加强了《平价医疗法案》，我们首次允许医疗保险为你们，美国人民，协商药品价格。

1220
01:24:36,787 --> 01:24:39,028
Donald Trump said he was going to allow Medicare to negotiate
唐纳德·特朗普说他将允许医疗保险协商

1221
01:24:40,068 --> 01:24:40,569
drug prices?
药品价格？

1222
01:24:40,609 --> 01:24:41,089
He never did.
他从未这样做。

1223
01:24:41,169 --> 01:24:41,490
We did.
我们做到了。

1224
01:24:42,030 --> 01:24:44,933
And now we have capped the cost of insulin at $35 a month.
现在我们已将胰岛素的价格上限定为每月35美元。

1225
01:24:45,213 --> 01:24:50,538
Since I've been vice president, we have capped the cost of prescription medication for seniors at $2,000 a year.
自从我担任副总统以来，我们已经将老年人处方药的费用上限定为每年2000美元。

1226
01:24:50,938 --> 01:24:57,083
And when I am president, we will do that for all people, understanding that the value I bring to this
当我成为总统时，我们将为所有人这样做，理解我带来的价值

1227
01:24:57,944 --> 01:25:04,146
is that access to health care should be a right and not just a privilege of those who can afford it.
是获得医疗保健应该是每个人的权利，而不仅仅是那些负担得起的人的特权。

1228
01:25:04,606 --> 01:25:13,449
And the plan has to be to strengthen the Affordable Care Act, not get rid of it, practice prologue in terms of where Donald Trump stands on that.
计划必须是加强《平价医疗法案》，而不是废除它，从唐纳德·特朗普在这方面的立场来看。

1229
01:25:13,489 --> 01:25:16,470
I want to move to an issue that's important for a lot of... You made a mistake.
我想转向一个对很多人来说都很重要的问题……你犯了一个错误。

1230
01:25:17,290 --> 01:25:21,371
At number one, John McCain fought Obamacare for 10 years.
首先，约翰·麦凯恩为《平价医疗法案》奋斗了10年。

1231
01:25:22,111 --> 01:25:23,272
But it wasn't only him.
但不仅仅是他。

1232
01:25:23,472 --> 01:25:26,433
It were all of the Democrats that kept it going.
是所有的民主党人一直在推动它。

1233
01:25:26,853 --> 01:25:27,433
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1234
01:25:28,837 --> 01:25:31,619
We can do much better than Obamacare, much less money.
我们可以做得比奥巴马医改更好，花更少的钱。

1235
01:25:31,979 --> 01:25:37,083
But she won't improve private insurance for people, private medical insurance.
但她不会改善人们的私人保险，私人医疗保险。

1236
01:25:37,784 --> 01:25:39,425
That's another thing she doesn't want to get.
这是她不想触及的另一个问题。

1237
01:25:39,445 --> 01:25:45,189
People are paying privately for insurance that have worked hard and made money and they want to have private.
人们努力工作赚钱，想要私人保险。

1238
01:25:45,389 --> 01:25:48,812
She wants everybody to be on government insurance where you wait.
她希望每个人都加入政府保险，在那里你要等待。

1239
01:25:49,372 --> 01:25:51,494
Six months for an operation that you need immediately.
需要立即手术的人要等六个月。

1240
01:25:51,514 --> 01:25:52,675
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢。

1241
01:25:52,735 --> 01:25:59,060
We have another issue that we'd like to get to that's important for a number of Americans, in particular younger voters, and that's climate change.
我们还有另一个对许多美国人来说重要的问题，特别是年轻选民，那就是气候变化。

1242
01:25:59,380 --> 01:26:04,144
President Trump, with regard to the environment, you say that we have to have clean air and clean water.
特朗普总统，关于环境，你说我们必须有清洁的空气和清洁的水。

1243
01:26:04,504 --> 01:26:08,207
Vice President Harris, you call climate change an existential threat.
哈里斯副总统，你称气候变化为生存威胁。

1244
01:26:08,587 --> 01:26:12,751
The question to you both tonight is what would you do to fight climate change?
今晚的问题是，你们两位将如何应对气候变化？

1245
01:26:12,871 --> 01:26:14,592
And Vice President Harris, we'll start with you.
哈里斯副总统，我们先从你开始。

1246
01:26:14,832 --> 01:26:15,673
One minute for you each.
每人一分钟。

1247
01:26:16,360 --> 01:26:19,461
Well, the former president had said that climate change is a hoax.
前总统曾说气候变化是个骗局。

1248
01:26:20,561 --> 01:26:22,822
And what we know is that it is very real.
我们知道这是非常真实的。

1249
01:26:22,962 --> 01:26:43,026
You ask anyone who lives in a state who has experienced these extreme weather occurrences, who now is either being denied home insurance or is being jacked up, you ask anybody who has been the victim of what that means in terms of losing their home, having nowhere to go, we know that we can actually deal with this issue.
问问那些经历过极端天气的人，现在要么被拒绝房屋保险，要么保费飙升，问问那些因失去家园、无处可去而受害的人，我们知道我们实际上可以处理这个问题。

1250
01:26:43,046 --> 01:26:45,727
The young people of America care deeply about this issue.
美国的年轻人非常关心这个问题。

1251
01:26:46,207 --> 01:26:58,436
And I am proud that as vice president over the last four years, we have invested a trillion dollars in a clean energy economy while we have also increased domestic gas production to historic levels.
我很自豪，作为副总统，过去四年我们投资了一万亿美元在清洁能源经济上，同时我们也增加了国内天然气产量到历史新高。

1252
01:26:58,876 --> 01:27:03,920
We have created over 800,000 new manufacturing jobs while I have been vice president.
在我担任副总统期间，我们创造了超过80万个新的制造业工作岗位。

1253
01:27:04,300 --> 01:27:10,465
We have invested in clean energy to the point that we are opening up factories around the world.
我们投资清洁能源，以至于我们在全球范围内开设工厂。

1254
01:27:10,485 --> 01:27:13,046
Donald Trump said he was going to create manufacturing jobs.
唐纳德·特朗普说他要创造制造业工作岗位。

1255
01:27:13,307 --> 01:27:14,768
He lost manufacturing jobs.
他失去了制造业工作岗位。

1256
01:27:15,248 --> 01:27:30,574
And I'm also proud to have the endorsement of the United Auto Workers and Sean Fain, who also know that part of building a clean energy economy includes investing in American-made products, American automobiles it includes.
我也自豪地获得了美国汽车工人联合会和肖恩·费恩的支持，他们也知道建设清洁能源经济的一部分包括投资美国制造的产品，包括美国汽车。

1257
01:27:31,394 --> 01:27:38,984
growing what we can do around American manufacturing and opening up auto plants, not closing them like happened under Donald Trump.
扩大我们在美国制造业的能力，开设汽车工厂，而不是像唐纳德·特朗普时期那样关闭它们。

1258
01:27:39,004 --> 01:27:40,525
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢。

1259
01:27:40,545 --> 01:27:41,867
That didn't happen under Donald Trump.
那不是在唐纳德·特朗普时期发生的。

1260
01:27:41,887 --> 01:27:46,132
Let me just tell you, they lost 10,000 manufacturing jobs this last month.
让我告诉你，上个月他们失去了1万个制造业工作岗位。

1261
01:27:46,773 --> 01:27:48,494
It's going, they're all leaving.
他们都在离开。

1262
01:27:49,174 --> 01:27:54,255
They're building big auto plants in Mexico, in many cases owned by China.
他们在墨西哥建大型汽车厂，很多时候是由中国拥有的。

1263
01:27:54,555 --> 01:28:01,157
They're building these massive plants and they think they're going to sell their cars into the United States because of these people.
他们建造这些巨大的工厂，认为他们会把这些车卖到美国，因为这些人。

1264
01:28:01,597 --> 01:28:05,739
What they have given to China is unbelievable, but we're not going to let that.
他们给中国的东西是难以置信的，但我们不会让这种情况继续。

1265
01:28:05,799 --> 01:28:10,200
We'll put tariffs on those cars so they can't come into our country because they will kill
我们会对这些车征收关税，这样他们就不能进入我们的国家，因为他们会摧毁

1266
01:28:10,720 --> 01:28:22,468
the United Auto Workers and any auto worker, whether it's in Detroit or South Carolina or any other place, what they've done to business and manufacturing in this country is horrible.
美国汽车工人联合会和任何汽车工人，无论是底特律还是南卡罗来纳州，或者其他任何地方，他们对我国商业和制造业的破坏是可怕的。

1267
01:28:22,888 --> 01:28:25,550
We have nothing because they refuse.
我们一无所有，因为他们拒绝。

1268
01:28:25,790 --> 01:28:30,453
You know, Biden doesn't go after people because supposedly China paid him millions of dollars.
你知道，拜登不追究某些人，据说是中国给了他数百万美元。

1269
01:28:30,493 --> 01:28:32,735
He's afraid to do it between him and his son.
他害怕这样做，因为他和他的儿子之间。

1270
01:28:33,175 --> 01:28:35,077
They get all this money from Ukraine.
他们从乌克兰得到所有这些钱。

1271
01:28:35,297 --> 01:28:37,899
They get all this money from all of these different countries.
他们从所有这些不同的国家得到所有这些钱。

1272
01:28:38,220 --> 01:28:42,183
And then you wonder, why is he so loyal to this one, that one, Ukraine, China?
然后你会想，为什么他对这个、那个、乌克兰、中国如此忠诚？

1273
01:28:42,603 --> 01:28:43,084
Why is he?
为什么他？

1274
01:28:43,304 --> 01:28:47,508
Why did he get $3.5 million from the mayor of Moscow's wife?
为什么他从莫斯科市长的妻子那里得到了350万美元？

1275
01:28:47,868 --> 01:28:51,611
Why did he get — why did she pay him $3.5 million?
为什么他得到了——为什么她付给他350万美元？

1276
01:28:52,232 --> 01:28:57,096
This is a crooked administration, and they're selling our country down the tubes.
这是一个腐败的政府，他们在把我们的国家卖掉。

1277
01:28:57,196 --> 01:28:58,277
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢你。

1278
01:28:58,537 --> 01:28:58,838
Thank you.
谢谢。

1279
01:28:59,198 --> 01:29:05,543
We'll be right back with closing statements from both of our candidates, an historic night, this ABC News presidential debate from Philadelphia.
我们马上回来，两位候选人将发表闭幕词，这是一个历史性的夜晚，这是ABC新闻在费城的总统辩论。

1280
01:29:05,603 --> 01:29:12,988
Back in a moment.
稍后回来。

1281
01:29:13,008 --> 01:29:17,011
The ABC News presidential debate will continue after this.
ABC新闻的总统辩论将继续进行。

1282
01:29:18,613 --> 01:29:26,659
Live from the National Constitution Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, here again, David Muir and Lindsay Davis.
从宾夕法尼亚州费城的美国宪法中心现场直播，再次由大卫·缪尔和林赛·戴维斯主持。

1283
01:29:27,571 --> 01:29:28,391
Welcome back tonight.
今晚欢迎回来。

1284
01:29:28,431 --> 01:29:30,052
The time has come for closing statements.
现在是闭幕词的时间。

1285
01:29:30,112 --> 01:29:31,853
And Vice President Harris, we begin with you.
哈里斯副总统，我们从你开始。

1286
01:29:33,813 --> 01:29:46,378
So I think you've heard tonight two very different visions for our country, one that is focused on the future and the other that is focused on the past and an attempt to take us backward.
所以我认为今晚你听到了两种截然不同的国家愿景，一种专注于未来，另一种则专注于过去，试图让我们倒退。

1287
01:29:48,032 --> 01:29:49,132
But we're not going back.
但我们不会倒退。

1288
01:29:49,933 --> 01:29:55,595
And I do believe that the American people know we all have so much more in common than what separates us.
我相信美国人民知道我们共同点远多于分歧。

1289
01:29:56,035 --> 01:29:58,736
And we can chart a new way forward.
我们可以开辟一条新的前进道路。

1290
01:29:59,536 --> 01:30:11,761
And a vision of that includes having a plan, understanding the aspirations, the dreams, the hopes, the ambition of the American people, which is why I intend to create
这个愿景包括有一个计划，理解美国人民的愿望、梦想、希望和抱负，这就是为什么我打算创造

1291
01:30:12,341 --> 01:30:27,021
an opportunity economy, investing in small businesses, in new families, in what we can do around protecting seniors, what we can do that is about giving hardworking folks a break and bringing down the cost of living.
机会经济，投资于小企业、新家庭，以及我们能为保护老年人所做的事情，为辛勤工作的人们减轻负担，降低生活成本。

1292
01:30:27,762 --> 01:30:45,266
I believe in what we can do together that is about sustaining America's standing in the world and ensuring that we have the respect that we so rightly deserve, including respecting our military and ensuring we have the most lethal fighting force in the world.
我相信我们能共同做的事情，是关于维持美国在世界上的地位，并确保我们得到应有的尊重，包括尊重我们的军队，确保我们拥有世界上最致命的战斗力量。

1293
01:30:45,906 --> 01:30:55,529
I will be a president that will protect our fundamental rights and freedoms, including the right of a woman to make decisions about her own body and not have her government tell her what to do.
我将是一位保护我们基本权利和自由的总统，包括女性对自己身体的决定权，而不是让政府告诉她该做什么。

1294
01:30:56,309 --> 01:30:59,150
I'll tell you, I started my career as a prosecutor.
我告诉你，我以检察官的身份开始了我的职业生涯。

1295
01:30:59,230 --> 01:31:03,731
I was a DA, I was an Attorney General, a United States Senator, and now Vice President.
我曾是地方检察官、总检察长、美国参议员，现在是副总统。

1296
01:31:03,791 --> 01:31:05,751
I've only had one client, the people.
我只有一个客户，那就是人民。

1297
01:31:06,471 --> 01:31:13,353
And I'll tell you, as a prosecutor, I never asked a victim or a witness, are you a Republican or a Democrat?
我告诉你，作为一名检察官，我从未问过受害者或证人，你是共和党人还是民主党人？

1298
01:31:14,033 --> 01:31:16,574
The only thing I ever asked them, are you okay?
我唯一问过他们的是，你还好吗？

1299
01:31:17,970 --> 01:31:24,793
And that's the kind of president we need right now, someone who cares about you and is not putting themselves first.
这就是我们现在需要的总统，一个关心你而不是把自己放在首位的人。

1300
01:31:25,674 --> 01:31:38,480
I intend to be a president for all Americans and focus on what we can do over the next 10 and 20 years to build back up our country by investing right now in you, the American people.
我打算成为所有美国人的总统，并专注于我们在未来10到20年里能做的事情，通过现在投资于你，美国人民，来重建我们的国家。

1301
01:31:39,000 --> 01:31:40,901
Vice President Harris, thank you.
副总统哈里斯，谢谢你。

1302
01:31:41,001 --> 01:31:41,662
President Trump?
特朗普总统？

1303
01:31:43,180 --> 01:31:48,364
So she just started by saying she's going to do this, she's going to do that, she's going to do all these wonderful things.
所以她一开始就说她要这样做，她要那样做，她要完成所有这些美好的事情。

1304
01:31:48,784 --> 01:31:50,505
Why hasn't she done it?
为什么她还没做？

1305
01:31:50,945 --> 01:31:53,047
She's been there for three and a half years.
她已经在那里三年半了。

1306
01:31:53,427 --> 01:31:56,149
They've had three and a half years to fix the border.
他们有三年半的时间来修复边境。

1307
01:31:56,549 --> 01:31:58,110
They've had three and a half years to
他们有三年半的时间来

1308
01:31:59,031 --> 01:32:01,373
create jobs, and all the things we talked about.
创造就业机会，以及我们谈论的所有事情。

1309
01:32:01,774 --> 01:32:03,635
Why hasn't she done it?
为什么她还没做？

1310
01:32:04,056 --> 01:32:11,382
She should leave right now, go down to that beautiful White House, go to the Capitol, get everyone together and do the things you want to do.
她现在应该离开，去那美丽的白宫，去国会，把所有人都召集起来，做你想做的事情。

1311
01:32:11,402 --> 01:32:17,028
But you haven't done it, and you won't do it, because you believe in things that the American people don't believe in.
但你没有做，而且你也不会做，因为你相信的事情是美国人民不相信的。

1312
01:32:17,488 --> 01:32:19,350
You believe in things like
你相信的事情比如

1313
01:32:19,690 --> 01:32:20,511
We're not going to frack.
我们不会进行水力压裂。

1314
01:32:20,591 --> 01:32:21,912
We're not going to take fossil fuel.
我们不会使用化石燃料。

1315
01:32:21,932 --> 01:32:26,795
We're not going to do things that are going to make this country strong, whether you like it or not.
我们不会做那些无论你喜欢与否都会让这个国家强大的事情。

1316
01:32:27,275 --> 01:32:28,296
Germany tried that.
德国试过那样。

1317
01:32:28,656 --> 01:32:33,440
And within one year, they were back to building normal energy plants.
一年之内，他们又回到了建设常规能源厂。

1318
01:32:33,740 --> 01:32:34,701
We're not ready for it.
我们还没准备好。

1319
01:32:35,021 --> 01:32:39,444
We can't sacrifice our country for the sake of bad vision.
我们不能为了糟糕的愿景而牺牲我们的国家。

1320
01:32:39,744 --> 01:32:41,586
But I just ask one simple question.
但我只问一个简单的问题。

1321
01:32:42,106 --> 01:32:43,907
Why didn't she do it?
她为什么不做？

1322
01:32:44,208 --> 01:32:45,448
We're a failing nation.
我们是一个正在衰败的国家。

1323
01:32:46,289 --> 01:32:48,930
We're a nation that's in serious decline.
我们是一个正在严重衰退的国家。

1324
01:32:49,230 --> 01:32:51,231
We're being laughed at all over the world.
全世界都在嘲笑我们。

1325
01:32:51,411 --> 01:32:52,531
All over the world, they laugh.
全世界都在嘲笑我们。

1326
01:32:52,631 --> 01:32:53,932
I know the leaders very well.
我非常了解这些领导人。

1327
01:32:53,972 --> 01:32:55,072
They're coming to see me.
他们来找我。

1328
01:32:55,392 --> 01:32:56,253
They call me.
他们给我打电话。

1329
01:32:56,673 --> 01:32:58,453
We're laughed at all over the world.
全世界都在嘲笑我们。

1330
01:32:58,493 --> 01:33:00,854
They don't understand what happened to us as a nation.
他们不明白我们国家发生了什么。

1331
01:33:01,174 --> 01:33:02,175
We're not a leader.
我们不是领导者。

1332
01:33:02,515 --> 01:33:04,716
We don't have any idea what's going on.
我们不知道发生了什么。

1333
01:33:05,056 --> 01:33:07,197
We have wars going on in the Middle East.
中东正在发生战争。

1334
01:33:07,237 --> 01:33:10,898
We have wars going on with Russia and Ukraine.
俄罗斯和乌克兰正在发生战争。

1335
01:33:11,258 --> 01:33:17,805
We're going to end up in a third world war and it'll be a war like no other because of nuclear weapons, the power of weaponry.
我们可能会陷入第三次世界大战，这将是一场前所未有的战争，因为核武器，武器的力量。

1336
01:33:18,405 --> 01:33:21,088
I rebuilt our entire military.
我重建了我们的整个军队。

1337
01:33:21,528 --> 01:33:24,531
She gave a lot of it away to the Taliban.
她把很多都给了塔利班。

1338
01:33:25,132 --> 01:33:26,693
She gave it to Afghanistan.
她给了阿富汗。

1339
01:33:27,094 --> 01:33:32,459
What these people have done to our country and maybe toughest of all is allowing millions of
这些人对我们国家所做的事情，也许最糟糕的是允许数百万人

1340
01:33:32,959 --> 01:33:34,720
people to come into our country.
进入我们的国家。

1341
01:33:34,820 --> 01:33:37,861
Many of them are criminals, and they're destroying our country.
他们中的许多人是罪犯，正在摧毁我们的国家。

1342
01:33:38,241 --> 01:33:43,503
The worst president, the worst vice president in the history of our country.
有史以来最糟糕的总统，最糟糕的副总统。

1343
01:33:43,843 --> 01:33:45,383
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢。

1344
01:33:45,523 --> 01:33:51,485
And that is our ABC News presidential debate from here in Philadelphia at the National Constitution Center.
这是我们在费城国家宪法中心为您带来的ABC新闻总统辩论。

1345
01:33:51,966 --> 01:33:52,706
I'm Lindsay Davis.
我是林赛·戴维斯。

1346
01:33:52,846 --> 01:33:53,646
And I'm David Muir.
我是大卫·缪尔。

1347
01:33:53,686 --> 01:33:55,087
Thank you for watching here in the U.S.
感谢您在美国和世界各地的观看，以及ABC新闻的全体工作人员。

1348
01:33:55,167 --> 01:33:57,848
and all over the world and from all of us here at ABC News.
晚安。

1349
01:33:58,388 --> 01:33:58,668
Good night.
谢谢观看。

1350
01:34:03,046 --> 01:34:03,868
Thanks for watching.
谢谢观看。

1351
01:34:03,988 --> 01:34:10,720
Stay updated about breaking news and top stories on the NBC News app or follow us on social media.
通过NBC新闻应用程序获取最新突发新闻和头条新闻，或在社交媒体上关注我们。

